      "text": "Residential plumbing is three independent pipe systems sharing the same walls:"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#003",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:plumbing:00-overview, git-history:plumbing:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "plumbing/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "plumbing/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:plumbing:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "plumbing",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "plumbing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Plumbing Systems - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                    PLUMBING SYSTEM OVERVIEW                      |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                  |\n|  SUPPLY SYSTEM              DWV SYSTEM           GAS SYSTEM      |\n|  =============              ==========           ==========      |\n|  Pressurized                Gravity-driven       Pressurized     |\n|  40–80 PSI                  1/4\" per foot slope  0.25–2 PSI      |\n|                                                                   |\n|  Municipal main             Fixtures drain        Gas meter       |\n|      ↓                          ↓                    ↓           |\n|  PRV (if needed)            Drain branches       Regulator       |\n|      ↓                          ↓                    ↓           |\n|  Water meter                P-trap (water seal)  Distribution    |\n|      ↓                          ↓                    ↓           |\n|  Cold main                  Horizontal drain     Branch lines    |\n|      ↓         ↓            (1/4\"/ft slope)          ↓           |\n|  Cold       Hot water       Vertical stack       Appliances      |\n|  fixtures   heater (120°F)      ↓               (furnace/range)  |\n|                             Building drain                        |\n|                                 ↓                                |\n|                             Sewer/septic                         |\n|                                                                  |\n|  VENT STACK (extends above roof — part of DWV)                   |\n|  Maintains atmospheric pressure; prevents trap siphon            |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#004",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:plumbing:00-overview, git-history:plumbing:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "plumbing/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "plumbing/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:plumbing:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
